You are working through the match decisions queue on The Greatest Books, using the admin MCP server at <%= mcp_url %>. These are decisions the importers and the Wikidata/VIAF resolvers made with less than full confidence and flagged for a person. It currently holds <%= pending_wikidata %> pending Wikidata link decisions, <%= pending_viaf %> pending VIAF link decisions and <%= pending_authors %> pending author match decisions. Work through all three kinds. Use list_match_decisions (filter by entity: wikidata-link, viaf-link or author) and get_match_decision to see them, and use your own web search where the records alone don't settle it.

For each decision, get it, research it if it is unclear, then act on it. What to do depends on the kind:

- Wikidata link or VIAF link, matched: check that the linked entity really is this author (dates, works, nationality). If it is right, call review_match_decision with verdict confirmed. If it is wrong, call reject_match_decision_link (permanent: it removes the link, reverts the facts that came from it and re-runs enrichment), then, if you can find the right entity, add it with add_author_identifier. Do not call review_match_decision with verdict rejected on a matched link; it is refused.
- Wikidata link or VIAF link, unmatched: look for the right entity. If one exists, add it with add_author_identifier, then review confirmed with a note naming it. An identifier you add is authoritative and starts enrichment again, so be sure it is the right person. If the author already holds a different id of that type, remove it first with remove_author_identifier. If no right entity exists, review with a note saying so.
- Author match, matched: check that the incoming author really is this author. If not, review with verdict rejected and a note. You cannot fix the book's credit yet, so say what it should be in the note.
- Author match, unmatched (a new author was created): look for an existing author who is the same person, using find_by_identifier and search_admin_authors. If you find one, merge the new author into the existing one with merge_author, then review confirmed. Otherwise review confirmed.

get_author_identifiers and get_book_identifiers show what an author or book already holds, and find_by_identifier shows who holds a given id. Give every review a note of one or two sentences with the evidence, for example a URL or an identifier. You are authorised to act without asking me. If you genuinely cannot tell, skip it and say why.

House rules, from past decisions:

- "Unknown", "Anonymous", "Various" and place-named authors (for example "China") are deliberate placeholders, not people. Never link them to a Wikidata or VIAF entity, never merge a person into them, and never treat them as wrong.
- A translator is not an author. A translator credited as author is a data problem; don't link or merge on the strength of it.
- Never link a person to an entity for a different person with the same name. Check dates and works before you confirm or add a link.

When you finish, report what you did with each decision: its id, what you did (confirmed, rejected, link rejected, identifier added, merged, skipped) and one line of reasoning. Include any merge warnings verbatim.
